":"G4151","lemma":"πνεῦμα","tr":"pneuma","gloss":"spirit","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":379}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":19,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"So the word of the Lord powerfully continued to spread and prevail.","from":7},{"book":"ACT","chapter":12,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"But the word of God continued to spread and multiply.","from":7},{"book":"1TI","chapter":3,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":15,"source":"openbible","text":"Furthermore, he must have a good reputation with outsiders, so that he will not fall into disgrace and into the snare of the devil.","from":3},{"book":"1TI","chapter":3,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":15,"source":"openbible","text":"in case I am delayed, so that you will know how each one must conduct himself in Godʼs household, which is the church of the living God, the pillar and foundation of the truth.","from":3},{"book":"ACT","chapter":1,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"With one accord they all continued in prayer, along with the women and Mary the mother of Jesus, and with His brothers.","from":4},{"book":"EXO","chapter":18,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"But Mosesʼ father-in-law said to him, “What you are doing is not good.","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":18,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":13,"source":"openbible","text":"And they judged the people at all times; they would bring the difficult cases to Moses, but any minor issue they would judge themselves.","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"At that time I said to you, “I cannot carry the burden for you alone.","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2}]},"8-15":{"people":[{"id":"stephen-g4736","name":"Stephen","kind":"person","brief":"Christian deacon","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":2,"firstVerse":11},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"places":[{"id":"alexandria-g0222","name":"Alexandria","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"asia-g0773","name":"Asia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"cilicia-g2791","name":"Cilicia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"cyrene-g2956","name":"Cyrene","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"nazareth-g3478","name":"Nazareth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"words":[{"base":"G4736","lemma":"Στέφανος","tr":"Stephanos","gloss":"Stephen","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"G2980","lemma":"λαλέω","tr":"laleō","gloss":"to speak","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":294},{"base":"G4892","lemma":"συνέδριον","tr":"sunedrion","gloss":"council","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":22},{"base":"G4487","lemma":"ῥῆμα","tr":"rhēma","gloss":"declaration","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":68},{"base":"G4383","lemma":"πρόσωπον","tr":"prosōpon","gloss":"face","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":76},{"base":"G3475","lemma":"Μωϋσῆς, Μωσῆς","tr":"Mōusēs, Mōsēs","gloss":"Moses","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":79},{"base":"G5117","lemma":"τόπος","tr":"topos","gloss":"place","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":94},{"base":"G2992","lemma":"λαός","tr":"laos","gloss":"a people","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":141},{"base":"G5037","lemma":"τε","tr":"te","gloss":"and","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":215},{"base":"G0221","lemma":"Ἀλεξανδρεύς","tr":"Alexandreus","gloss":"Alexandrian","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LUK","chapter":21,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"For I will give you speech and wisdom that none of your adversaries will be able to resist or contradict.","from":10},{"book":"MAT","chapter":13,"verse":43,"verseEnd":43,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Then the righteous will shine like the sun in the kingdom of their Father. He who has ears, let him hear.","from":15},{"book":"ACT","chapter":4,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"And now, Lord, consider their threats, and enable Your servants to speak Your word with complete boldness,","from":8},{"book":"ACT","chapter":4,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"as You stretch out Your hand to heal and perform signs and wonders through the name of Your holy servant Jesus.”","from":8},{"book":"ECC","chapter":8,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Who is like the wise man? Who knows the interpretation of a matter? A manʼs wisdom brightens his face, and the sternness of his face is changed.","from":15},{"book":"1CO","chapter":2,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"My message and my preaching were not with persuasive words of wisdom, but with a demonstration of the Spiritʼs power,","from":10},{"book":"JOB","chapter":32,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"But there is a spirit in a man, the breath of the Almighty, that gives him understanding.","from":10},{"book":"MAT","chapter":10,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"But when they hand you over, do not worry about how to respond or what to say. In that hour you will be given what to say.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2}]}}